  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The option \"arc turns at corners\" (`blend_turns`) gets a radius, `blend_radius`.\n  - No radius means the tool radius. This is the radius that every earlier file used. The default output does not change, and no golden changes.\n  - The radius must be at least 0.01 mm and no more than the tool radius. The command door refuses a radius under 0.01 mm by name. The generator refuses a radius larger than the tool radius by name.\n  - The fillet tally states the corner rest of a smaller radius, as before.\n- Kinds that have the option and the radius now:\n  - 2D Pocket (the radius is new).\n  - 2D Adaptive (the option and the radius are new). The Trochoidal method refuses the option by name, because its loops are arcs already.\n  - 2D Offset (the option and the radius are new).\n- The project file writes the two keys only when they are set. The stamp digest takes them only when they are set, so existing operations do not become Stale.\n- MCP `edit_operation`: `{\"blend_turns\": false}` was refused as an unknown field, because the flag is written only when ON. A `false` value is now kept when the field exists. A misspelled field is still refused.\n- UI: the 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive and 2D Offset pages show the option and a radius row. The radius seeds 0.5 mm. A warning shows when the option is on with the Trochoidal method.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/1733-arc-turns.md`.\n\nKinds not covered (follow-up #1759):\n- Slot. Open PR #1745 changes Slot. This PR does not touch Slot, so the two PRs do not conflict.\n- Face and 2D Contour.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/motion/tests/corner_arc_radius.rs` (7 tests):\n  - `corners_turn_on_tangent_arcs_of_the_given_radius` (Zigzag, Waterline and Offset rings, with an island)\n  - `no_arc_turn_cuts_past_the_wall`\n  - `the_corner_rest_is_stated_and_shrinks_with_the_radius`\n  - `no_radius_is_the_tool_radius_every_earlier_file_blends_at`\n  - `with_the_option_off_the_radius_changes_nothing`\n  - `the_door_refuses_a_radius_no_control_can_cut_by_name`\n  - `the_adaptive_spiral_turns_on_arcs_of_the_radius_inside_the_wall`\n- New `crates/app/tests/arc_turn_params.rs` (4 tests):\n  - `the_three_kinds_take_arc_turns_and_a_radius_through_edit_operation_and_undo`\n  - `a_radius_no_control_can_cut_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `arc_turns_beside_the_trochoidal_method_are_refused_by_name`\n  - `the_project_file_keeps_the_radius_and_a_default_file_has_no_key`\n- About 40 existing test files get the new fields in their struct literals (`blend_radius: None`, `blend_turns: false`). No assertion changed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`:\n  - motion suites: ok.\n  - app suites: 430 of 431 binaries ok. `winding_align::the_inside_out_stl_fixture_reads_inside_out_and_refuses` fails. This failure is on main too (issue #1752, fix in PR #1761). This PR does not touch import or winding code.\n  - ui suites (CWD `crates/ui`, the same command as the gate plan): ok, 847 tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not opened. The new UI rows are not seen by a person. Before and after screenshots of the three operation pages are owed.\n- The 2D Adaptive test uses a small rectangle (16 x 12 mm). On that part the generator uses Offset rings. One debug run on the island fixture takes about 15 s.\n- No post output was examined by a person. The goldens and the recorded post streams did not change.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill does not list the new `blend_radius` field yet. That file is a process file, so it is left out of this PR.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive and 2D Offset: arc turns at corners take a corner arc radius (default: the tool radius, output unchanged) (#1733)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1733\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
